@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · 环境要求：- DeepSeek Harness `0.2.2-alpha.2` 或更高。这是**最低支持版本**（本插件就是按这一版构建和测试的），不是「当前版本」：低于它的没验证过，**上限不设**——插件跟着 DSH 更新，升级 DSH 之后装最新版即可。加载失败时先按「常见问题」里的说明处理。
- Web 端（命令行起的 `dsh web`）另需 Node.js `^22.19.0` 或 `>= 24.0.0`，以及 pnpm 10 或更高。
- **桌面应用不需要你另装 Node 和 pnpm**：它自带这两样，包操作走它自己的运行时。

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · Web 端：```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add @firetruck666/dsh-task-board
```

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · Requirements：- DeepSeek Harness `0.2.2-alpha.2` or later. This is the **minimum supported version** (the release the plugin is built and tested against), not "the current one": anything older is untested, and there is no upper bound — the plugin is updated alongside DSH, so just install the latest build after upgrading DSH. If loading fails, follow the Troubleshooting section.
- For the web GUI (a `dsh web` you started yourself): Node.js `^22.19.0` or `>= 24.0.0`, and pnpm 10 or newer.
- The **desktop app needs neither**: it ships its own Node and pnpm and runs package operations on its own runtime.

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · The web GUI：```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add @firetruck666/dsh-task-board
```

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · Nothing to configure by hand：The one step you must take is **restarting that surface** (the host half lives in the server process and is not loaded otherwise). All three install routes — npm, GitHub, local — behave identically here, and so do the two surfaces.

This plugin has no settings and needs no settings panel: the board's behavior (tasks, schedules, cruise, rules) is edited directly on the board, and on/off is the switch above.

To remove it:

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · Updating：The board header's right toolbar has a permanent **Check for updates** button. One click answers
three questions: **which copy is running** (which profile, where it lives, how it was installed),
**whether there is a newer one**, and **how to get it**.

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · One workbench, three pages：The sidebar carries **Overview**, **Task board** and **Task list**, and the three share one navigation
bar at the top — so which page you are on, and how much is waiting on each of the others, is visible
at a glance.

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · The board：Five columns, and reading them left to right is the whole life of a piece of work: Backlog / To do /
In progress / In Review / Done. Drag a card between columns, or up and down inside one to set the
order.

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · Automation, several devices, and the AI doors：**What the words on a card mean.**
The five columns are **Backlog / To do / In progress / In Review / Done**. They all read
from **one derivation**, so the same card gives the same answer wherever you see it:

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · Design system preview：```sh
DSH_TASK_BOARD_DESIGN_PREVIEW=1 pnpm dsh web   # or add that variable to however you start it
```

@firetruck666/dsh-task-board README · Troubleshooting：If the row is **not there at all**: the page is probably still serving an older bundle, so refresh;
if that does not help, check whether **Task List** is off on the plugin's own page — the plugin page
lists this plugin's rows, and turning that one off does not affect the board.
